  "final_message": "I have started running the test suite to establish a baseline. Waiting for the tests to finish.\nI'll check the search results once the command completes.\nI'll wait for the directory listing.\nI will wait for the search across all TypeScript files to finish.\nI will wait for git status and log to complete.\nI will wait for the git commit log.\nI will wait for the search for ARCH and deprecation references.\nI will wait for git branches and stash check to complete.\nRemoving `channel` directly from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract Compatibility**: Even if `channel` is no longer actively read by internal logic, deployed consumers in other repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) depend on the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) schema. Field removals cannot be made directly without a deprecation process.\n2. **Coupling with the Order Model**: The [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) domain model supplies data to [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59). Removing `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) while preserving [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) would require either populating a dummy/default value or transitioning the field through a formal deprecation phase across repositories.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\nTo retire the `channel` field compliant with ARCH-4:\n1. Coordinate deprecation with the consumer teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n2. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` (or optional/nullable if permitted by consumer schemas).\n3. Schedule removal in a future major schema version once consumers have safely decoupled.\n",
